# gameover.script — deterministic path to the game-over/hi-score screen.
#
# Derived EMPIRICALLY on this pre-task-10 tree (seed 12345): with an idle ship
# (no input after 's'), seeded rocks + enemy saucers destroy all 3 ships; the
# last life is lost between boundaries ~1100-1200 and the hi-score screen is
# byte-stable from boundary ~1200 on (compare -metric AE = 0 across
# g1200..g1800 probes). The capture at 1800 sits well past the freeze; once
# the tree is static, later captures are pixel-identical by construction.
#
# Requires: --hiscore test/harness/fixtures/hiScore.nul.data — the NUL-format
# encoding of qa/fixtures/hiScore.data. The committed fixture is whitespace-
# delimited, which the PRE-task-10 reader cannot parse: score.H's custom
# operator>>(ifstream&, char*) consumes names up to a NUL byte, so against the
# whitespace fixture it yields numScores=1, a mangled name, and an
# UNINITIALIZED score[0] rendered as per-run garbage digits (non-deterministic
# by construction). See qa/baseline-x11/MANIFEST.
#
# Run:
#   ./obj/harness --seed 12345 --script test/harness/scripts/gameover.script \
#                 --out <dir> --hiscore test/harness/fixtures/hiScore.nul.data

1 keydown s
4 keyup s
60  capture game_start
1800 capture hiscore
